#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:4
msgid "格子振動の熱的性質"
msgstr "Thermal Properties of Lattice Vibrations"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:6
msgid ""
"\\ :ref:`調和近似<harmonic-approximation>`\\ では、結晶の振動は独立な調和振動子の集まり（\\ "
":ref:`基準振動<ph-normal-modes>`）に分かれる。 "
"本稿では、量子化した振動子のエネルギーから、絶対零度でも残る零点振動と、有限温度の振動エネルギー・比熱・ "
"自由エネルギーを求める。続いて、2次の展開を超える非調和性と、振動数の体積依存性から生じる熱膨張を "
"準調和近似で扱い、この近似を使える条件を確かめる。"
msgstr ""
"In the \\ :ref:`harmonic approximation <harmonic-approximation>`\\ , "
"crystal vibrations separate into independent harmonic oscillators (\\ "
":ref:`normal modes <ph-normal-modes>`). From the quantized oscillator "
"energies, we obtain the zero-point vibrations that persist at absolute "
"zero and the vibrational energy, heat capacity, and free energy at finite"
" temperature. We then use the quasi-harmonic approximation to treat "
"anharmonicity beyond the quadratic expansion and thermal expansion due to"
" the volume dependence of the frequencies. We also examine the conditions"
" under which the approximation applies."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:11
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`調和近似とフォノン<phonon>`\\ （とくに\\ :ref:`基準振動とフォノン<ph-normal-"
"modes>`、:ref:`虚数振動数と動的安定性<imaginary-frequency>`）、 "
":ref:`エネルギー等分配<temperature>`、統計力学のカノニカル分布。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Harmonic Approximation and Phonons <phonon>`\\  "
"(especially \\ :ref:`Normal Modes and Phonons <ph-normal-modes>` and "
":ref:`Imaginary Frequencies and Dynamical Stability <imaginary-"
"frequency>`), :ref:`Energy Equipartition <temperature>`, and the "
"canonical distribution in statistical mechanics."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:14
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:16
msgid "零点エネルギーと零点振動を調和振動子の量子効果として求め、構造の安定性の順序や転移温度に影響しうることを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Obtain zero-point energy and zero-point vibrations as quantum effects of "
"the harmonic oscillator and explain how they can affect the stability "
"ordering of structures and transition temperatures."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:17
msgid "Bose–Einstein分布からモードの平均エネルギーと比熱を求め、高温で古典論の値に近づくことを示す。"
msgstr ""
"Use the Bose–Einstein distribution to obtain the mean energy and heat "
"capacity of a mode and show that they approach their classical values at "
"high temperature."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:18
msgid "分配関数から振動の自由エネルギーを導き、準調和近似で熱膨張とGrüneisen定数を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Derive the vibrational free energy from the partition function and use "
"the quasi-harmonic approximation to explain thermal expansion and the "
"Grüneisen parameter."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:19
msgid "準調和近似を使える条件と、非調和性をあらわに扱う必要がある場合を区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Distinguish the conditions in which the quasi-harmonic approximation "
"applies from those that require an explicit treatment of anharmonicity."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:24
msgid "零点振動と零点エネルギー"
msgstr "Zero-Point Vibrations and Zero-Point Energy"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:26
msgid "調和振動子の基底状態のエネルギーは0でなく :math:`\\hbar\\omega/2` である。結晶全体では"
msgstr ""
"A harmonic oscillator has a nonzero ground-state energy of "
":math:`\\hbar\\omega/2`. For the crystal as a whole, the sum"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:28
msgid ""
"E_{\\mathrm{ZP}}=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)"
msgstr ""
"E_{\\mathrm{ZP}}=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:33
msgid ""
"が絶対零度でも残り、これを **零点エネルギー** と呼ぶ。基底状態の振幅の2乗平均は :math:`\\langle "
"Q^2\\rangle=\\hbar/(2\\omega)` であり、原子は0 Kでも平衡位置のまわりに広がっている "
"（**零点振動**）。:math:`Q` は質量の平方根を含むので、質量 :math:`m` の原子1個だけが動く モードでは変位の2乗平均が "
":math:`\\hbar/(2m\\omega)` になり、軽い原子や振動数の低いモードほど大きい。"
msgstr ""
"persists even at absolute zero and is called the **zero-point energy**. "
"The mean square amplitude in the ground state is :math:`\\langle "
"Q^2\\rangle=\\hbar/(2\\omega)`, so the atoms are spread around their "
"equilibrium positions even at 0 K (**zero-point vibrations**). The "
"coordinate :math:`Q` includes the square root of the mass, so if only one"
" atom of mass :math:`m` moves in a mode, its mean square displacement is "
":math:`\\hbar/(2m\\omega)`. This value is larger for lighter atoms or "
"lower-frequency modes."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:38
msgid ""
"零点エネルギーは構造ごとに異なるので、静止した原子で計算した全エネルギーの差が小さい二つの 構造では、:eq:`ph-zpe` "
"の差で安定性の順序が変わることがある。原子核の量子揺らぎは、 "
"相転移の温度も変える。ZhongとVanderbiltは、第一原理計算に基づく有効ハミルトニアンを 経路積分モンテカルロ法で解いた "
"[Zhong1996]_。SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では量子揺らぎが強誘電転移を完全に抑え、:ref:`八面体回転<sm-"
"octahedral-rotation>`\\ の転移温度を130 Kから110 Kに下げた。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"では転移温度が35〜50 K下がった。"
msgstr ""
"The zero-point energy differs from one structure to another. When two "
"structures have nearly equal total energies with the atoms held "
"stationary, the difference in their zero-point energies (Equation :eq"
":`ph-zpe`) can change their stability ordering. Quantum fluctuations of "
"the nuclei also change phase transition temperatures. Zhong and "
"Vanderbilt solved an effective Hamiltonian based on first-principles "
"calculations using path-integral Monte Carlo [Zhong1996]_. In SrTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ , quantum fluctuations completely suppressed the ferroelectric"
" transition and lowered the :ref:`octahedral rotation <sm-octahedral-"
"rotation>`\\  transition temperature from 130 K to 110 K. In BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ , they lowered the transition temperatures by 35–50 K."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:46
msgid "有限温度の振動エネルギーと比熱"
msgstr "Vibrational Energy and Heat Capacity at Finite Temperature"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:48
msgid ""
"温度 :math:`T` では、振動数 :math:`\\omega` のモードの平均エネルギーは、**Bose–Einstein分布** の "
"占有数 :math:`n_{\\mathrm B}=1/(e^{\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm B}T}-1)` を使って"
msgstr ""
"At temperature :math:`T`, the mean energy of a mode of frequency "
":math:`\\omega` follows from the **Bose–Einstein distribution** with "
"occupation number :math:`n_{\\mathrm B}=1/(e^{\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T}-1)`:"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:51
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\langle E\\rangle=\\hbar\\omega\\left(n_{\\mathrm B}+\\frac12\\right)"
msgstr "\\langle E\\rangle=\\hbar\\omega\\left(n_{\\mathrm B}+\\frac12\\right)"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:56
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`x=\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm B}T` が小さい高温では "
":math:`1/(e^x-1)=1/x-1/2+x/12+O(x^3)` より :math:`\\langle "
"E\\rangle=k_{\\mathrm B}T+(\\hbar\\omega)^2/(12k_{\\mathrm B}T)+\\cdots` "
"で、主要項は古典論の\\ :ref:`エネルギー等分配<temperature>`\\ の値 :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T` "
"に一致する。 :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ll\\hbar\\omega` "
"の低温では、モードはほぼ基底状態にとどまり、温度を上げても エネルギーがほとんど増えない。"
msgstr ""
"At high temperatures, where :math:`x=\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm B}T` is "
"small, :math:`1/(e^x-1)=1/x-1/2+x/12+O(x^3)` gives :math:`\\langle "
"E\\rangle=k_{\\mathrm B}T+(\\hbar\\omega)^2/(12k_{\\mathrm B}T)+\\cdots`."
" The leading term agrees with the classical \\ :ref:`energy equipartition"
" <temperature>`\\  value :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T`. At low temperatures "
"with :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ll\\hbar\\omega`, the mode stays close to "
"its ground state and its energy barely increases as the temperature "
"rises."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:64
msgid "モードの平均エネルギーを温度で微分すると、そのモードの定積熱容量が求まる。結晶全体では"
msgstr ""
"Differentiating the mean energy of a mode with respect to temperature "
"gives that mode's constant-volume heat capacity. For the whole crystal,"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:66
msgid ""
"C_V=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k,s}k_{\\mathrm "
"B}\\frac{x_s^2e^{x_s}}{(e^{x_s}-1)^2},\\qquad\n"
"x_s=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}"
msgstr ""
"C_V=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k,s}k_{\\mathrm "
"B}\\frac{x_s^2e^{x_s}}{(e^{x_s}-1)^2},\\qquad\n"
"x_s=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:72
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`x_s\\to0` の高温では各モードの寄与が :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}` に近づき、:math:`n` "
"原子の単位胞を :math:`N_{\\mathrm c}` 個並べた結晶全体で :math:`3nN_{\\mathrm "
"c}k_{\\mathrm B}`、すなわち原子1個あたり :math:`3k_{\\mathrm B}` になる "
"（Dulong–Petitの法則）。:math:`x_s\\gg1` の低温のモードは基底状態にとどまるので、寄与は "
":math:`k_{\\mathrm B}x_s^2e^{-x_s}` と指数関数的に小さくなり、 "
"比熱はDulong–Petitの値より小さくなる。 "
"ただし3次元の結晶には、Γ点の近くで振動数が0に近づく音響分枝があるので、どんな低温でも励起されるモードが残る。 "
"そのため低温の比熱は指数関数的ではなく、:math:`T^3` に比例して減る（Debyeの :math:`T^3` 則）。"
msgstr ""
"At high temperatures, where :math:`x_s\\to0`, each mode's contribution "
"approaches :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}`. For a crystal with :math:`n` atoms per"
" unit cell and :math:`N_{\\mathrm c}` cells, the total approaches "
":math:`3nN_{\\mathrm c}k_{\\mathrm B}`, or :math:`3k_{\\mathrm B}` per "
"atom (the Dulong–Petit law). At low temperatures with :math:`x_s\\gg1`, "
"the mode remains in its ground state, so its contribution becomes "
"exponentially small, :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}x_s^2e^{-x_s}`, and the heat "
"capacity falls below the Dulong–Petit value. However, a three-dimensional"
" crystal has acoustic branches whose frequencies approach zero near the Γ"
" point, so some modes are excited at arbitrarily low temperatures. As a "
"result, the heat capacity decreases in proportion to :math:`T^3` at low "
"temperatures, rather than exponentially (the Debye :math:`T^3` law)."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:82
msgid "振動の自由エネルギー"
msgstr "Vibrational Free Energy"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:84
msgid ""
"振動数 :math:`\\omega` の調和振動子の分配関数は、エネルギー :math:`\\hbar\\omega(n+1/2)` "
"の等比級数の和"
msgstr ""
"For a harmonic oscillator of frequency :math:`\\omega` the partition "
"function is a geometric sum over the energy levels "
":math:`\\hbar\\omega(n+1/2)`:"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:86
msgid ""
"Z=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}e^{-\\hbar\\omega(n+1/2)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\n"
"=\\frac{e^{-\\hbar\\omega/2k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T}}{1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm B}T}}"
msgstr ""
"Z=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}e^{-\\hbar\\omega(n+1/2)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\n"
"=\\frac{e^{-\\hbar\\omega/2k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T}}{1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega/k_{\\mathrm B}T}}"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:91
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"である。独立なモードの自由エネルギーは足し合わせられるので、:math:`F=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ln Z` から、振動の "
"自由エネルギーは"
msgstr ""
"The free energies of independent modes add, so :math:`F=-k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T\\ln Z` gives the vibrational free energy"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:94
msgid ""
"F_{\\mathrm{vib}}(T)=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\left[\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)\n"
"+k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ln\\left(1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right)\\right]"
msgstr ""
"F_{\\mathrm{vib}}(T)=\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\left[\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k)\n"
"+k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ln\\left(1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right)\\right]"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:100
msgid ""
"となる。和は、Γ点の音響分枝の3モードを除いてとる。これらは結晶全体の剛体並進で、安定な結晶でも :math:`\\omega=0` であり、 "
"振動ではない。Γ点を含むk点メッシュでこの3モードを和に入れると、第2項の対数が発散する。 第1項は零点エネルギー :eq:`ph-zpe` "
"で、第2項は負なので、温度が上がると :math:`F_{\\mathrm{vib}}` は下がる。 "
"振動数の低いモードほど第2項が大きく負になるので、振動数の低いモードを多くもつ構造ほど、温度とともに "
"自由エネルギーが相対的に下がる。振動のエントロピーは :math:`S_{\\mathrm{vib}}=-\\partial "
"F_{\\mathrm{vib}}/\\partial T` で求まる。 "
"静止した原子の全エネルギーの差が小さい二つの構造では、この項で有限温度の安定性の順序が入れ替わることがある。"
msgstr ""
"Exclude the three modes of the acoustic branches at the Γ point from the "
"sum. These are rigid translations of the entire crystal with "
":math:`\\omega=0` even in a stable crystal, so they are not vibrations. "
"Including them when the k-point mesh contains the Γ point makes the "
"logarithm in the second term diverge. The first term is the zero-point "
"energy (Equation :eq:`ph-zpe`), and the second term is negative, so "
":math:`F_{\\mathrm{vib}}` decreases as the temperature rises. The lower "
"the frequency of a mode, the more negative its second term. As the "
"temperature rises, the free energy falls farther for structures with more"
" low-frequency modes. The vibrational entropy is given by "
":math:`S_{\\mathrm{vib}}=-\\partial F_{\\mathrm{vib}}/\\partial T`. If "
"two structures have nearly equal total energies with the atoms held "
"stationary, this term can reverse their stability ordering at finite "
"temperature."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:110
msgid "非調和性"
msgstr "Anharmonicity"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:112
msgid ""
":eq:`ph-expansion` で無視した3次以上の項を **非調和項** と呼ぶ。非調和項があると 基準振動 :eq:`ph-"
"normal-modes` は互いに独立でなくなり、フォノンどうしがエネルギーをやり取りする。 "
"その結果、フォノンは有限の寿命をもち、熱伝導率が有限になる。振動の振幅が温度とともに "
"大きくなると、平均的な力定数が変わり、振動数も温度に依存する。"
msgstr ""
"The cubic and higher-order terms neglected in Equation :eq:`ph-expansion`"
" are called **anharmonic terms**. In their presence, the normal modes of "
"Equation :eq:`ph-normal-modes` are no longer independent, and phonons "
"exchange energy. As a result, phonons have finite lifetimes and the "
"thermal conductivity is finite. As the vibrational amplitudes increase "
"with temperature, the average force constants change and the frequencies "
"also become temperature dependent."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:117
msgid ""
"虚数振動数をもつ構造でも、エネルギーが際限なく下がるわけではない。調和近似の :math:`\\frac12\\omega_s^2Q^2` "
"は小さい :math:`Q` での形にすぎず、変位が大きくなると4次などの "
"非調和項がエネルギーを押し上げる。曲率が負の原点と、大きい変位での壁の間に、 エネルギーの極小が現れる。この形を\\ "
":ref:`二重井戸ポテンシャル<double-well-potential>`\\ と呼び、虚数振動数をもつモードが 低温で凍結する\\ "
":ref:`ソフトモード<soft-mode>`\\ の考え方につながる。"
msgstr ""
"Even for a structure with an imaginary frequency, the energy does not "
"decrease without bound. The harmonic approximation gives the form "
":math:`\\frac12\\omega_s^2Q^2`, which applies only at small :math:`Q`. At"
" larger displacements, anharmonic terms such as the quartic term drive "
"the energy back up. An energy minimum appears between the origin, where "
"the curvature is negative, and the wall at large displacement. This shape"
" is called a \\ :ref:`double-well potential <double-well-potential>`\\  "
"and leads to the concept of a \\ :ref:`soft mode <soft-mode>`\\ , in "
"which a mode with an imaginary frequency freezes in at low temperature."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:126
msgid "熱膨張と準調和近似"
msgstr "Thermal Expansion and the Quasi-Harmonic Approximation"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:128
msgid ""
"厳密に調和的な結晶は熱膨張しない。力定数が体積によらなければ振動数も体積によらず、 "
"振動の自由エネルギーは体積の関数にならないので、平衡体積は温度で変わらない。 原子の平均位置も、放物線のポテンシャルでは平衡位置からずれない。"
msgstr ""
"A strictly harmonic crystal exhibits no thermal expansion. If the force "
"constants are independent of volume, so are the frequencies. The "
"vibrational free energy is then independent of volume, and the "
"equilibrium volume does not change with temperature. In a parabolic "
"potential, the average atomic positions also stay at their equilibrium "
"positions."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:132
msgid ""
"**準調和近似** では、各体積で調和近似を使い、振動数の体積依存性だけを取り入れる。 静止した原子の全エネルギー :math:`U(V)` "
"に、各体積の振動数で求めた振動の自由エネルギー :eq:`ph-vib-free-energy` を加えた"
msgstr ""
"The **quasi-harmonic approximation** applies the harmonic approximation "
"at each volume and accounts only for the volume dependence of the "
"frequencies. The total free energy is the sum of the static total energy "
":math:`U(V)` and the vibrational free energy (Equation :eq:`ph-vib-free-"
"energy`) evaluated at the frequencies for each volume:"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:135
msgid ""
"F(V,T)=U(V)+\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\left[\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k;V)\n"
"+k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ln\\left(1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k;V)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right)\\right]"
msgstr ""
"F(V,T)=U(V)+\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k,s}\\left[\\frac12\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol k;V)\n"
"+k_{\\mathrm B}T\\ln\\left(1-e^{-\\hbar\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k;V)/k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right)\\right]"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:141
msgid ""
"を、外圧が0の場合に体積について最小にすると、温度 :math:`T` での平衡体積が求まる。和は式 :eq:`ph-vib-free-"
"energy` と同じく、Γ点の剛体並進の3モードを除いてとる。 外圧 :math:`P_{\\mathrm{ext}}` "
"がかかっている場合は、:math:`F+P_{\\mathrm{ext}}V` を最小にする [Baroni2010]_。 角括弧の中を "
":math:`\\omega` で微分すると :math:`\\hbar(n_{\\mathrm B}+1/2)=\\langle "
"E\\rangle/\\omega` になるので、モードごとの **Grüneisen定数**"
msgstr ""
"At zero external pressure, minimizing this expression with respect to "
"volume gives the equilibrium volume at temperature :math:`T`. As in "
"Equation :eq:`ph-vib-free-energy`, exclude the three Γ-point rigid "
"translations from the sum. Under an external pressure "
":math:`P_{\\mathrm{ext}}`, minimize :math:`F+P_{\\mathrm{ext}}V` "
"[Baroni2010]_. Differentiating the expression in brackets with respect to"
" :math:`\\omega` gives :math:`\\hbar(n_{\\mathrm B}+1/2)=\\langle "
"E\\rangle/\\omega`. For each mode, the **Grüneisen parameter** is"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:147
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\gamma_s(\\boldsymbol k)=-\\frac{\\partial\\ln\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)}{\\partial\\ln V}"
msgstr ""
"\\gamma_s(\\boldsymbol k)=-\\frac{\\partial\\ln\\omega_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)}{\\partial\\ln V}"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:152
msgid "を使うと、圧力 :math:`P=-\\partial F/\\partial V` は"
msgstr "With this parameter, the pressure :math:`P=-\\partial F/\\partial V` is"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:154
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P=-\\frac{dU}{dV}+\\frac1V\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k,s}\\gamma_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\,\\langle E_s(\\boldsymbol k)\\rangle"
msgstr ""
"P=-\\frac{dU}{dV}+\\frac1V\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k,s}\\gamma_s(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\,\\langle E_s(\\boldsymbol k)\\rangle"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:159
msgid ""
"となる。第2項は振動による圧力である。体積を広げると振動数が下がる（:math:`\\gamma>0`）通常の固体では "
"この項が正で、結晶は外へ押し広げられる。温度が上がると :math:`\\langle E\\rangle` が増えて体積が "
"大きくなる。:math:`\\langle E\\rangle` には零点エネルギーも含まれるので、0 Kでも平衡体積は "
"静止した原子の値より少し大きい。:math:`U(V)` を平衡体積のまわりで体積弾性率 :math:`B` を使って展開し、 "
"すべてのモードが同じ :math:`\\gamma` をもつとすると、熱膨張係数は :math:`\\alpha\\simeq\\gamma "
"C_V/(BV)`\\ （:math:`C_V` は式 :eq:`ph-heat-capacity` "
"の定積熱容量）となる。これをGrüneisenの関係と呼ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"The second term is the pressure due to vibrations. In typical solids, "
"frequencies decrease as volume increases (:math:`\\gamma>0`), so this "
"term is positive and pushes the crystal outward. As temperature rises, "
":math:`\\langle E\\rangle` increases and the volume grows. Because "
":math:`\\langle E\\rangle` includes the zero-point energy, the "
"equilibrium volume is slightly greater than the static value even at 0 K."
" If we expand :math:`U(V)` about the equilibrium volume using the bulk "
"modulus :math:`B` and assume that all modes have the same "
":math:`\\gamma`, the thermal expansion coefficient is "
":math:`\\alpha\\simeq\\gamma C_V/(BV)`\\  (:math:`C_V` is the constant-"
"volume heat capacity from Equation :eq:`ph-heat-capacity`). This is the "
"Grüneisen relation."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:168
msgid ""
"準調和近似は振動数の体積依存性だけを取り込み、一定体積でのフォノンどうしの相互作用は 無視する。式 :eq:`ph-qha-free-"
"energy` の対数は、Γ点の剛体並進の3モードを除いた残りのすべてのモードで :math:`\\omega^2>0` のときにだけ "
"定義できるので、この近似を使えるのは、考える体積の範囲で\\ :ref:`動的に安定<imaginary-frequency>`\\ "
"な構造に限る。 安定性も、剛体並進を除いた残りのモードで判定する。 温度が高く振幅が大きい場合や、0 "
"Kの計算で虚数振動数をもつ構造には、そのままでは使えない。"
msgstr ""
"The quasi-harmonic approximation accounts only for the volume dependence "
"of the frequencies and neglects phonon–phonon interactions at fixed "
"volume. The logarithm in Equation :eq:`ph-qha-free-energy` is defined "
"only when :math:`\\omega^2>0` for all modes other than the three Γ-point "
"rigid translations, so the approximation applies only to structures that "
"are \\ :ref:`dynamically stable <imaginary-frequency>`\\  over the range "
"of volumes considered. Assess stability using the modes left after "
"excluding rigid translations. The approximation cannot be used as is at "
"high temperatures with large vibrational amplitudes or for structures "
"with imaginary frequencies in a 0 K calculation."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:177
msgid "説明用の事例：BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の格子定数の計算値と実験値"
msgstr ""
"Worked Example: Calculated and Experimental Values of the Lattice "
"Constants of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:179
msgid ""
"`計算事例「格子定数」 <https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/lattice-"
"constant.html>`_\\ は、4相の格子定数をDFT（OpenMX、Quantum "
"ESPRESSO）と機械学習原子間ポテンシャルで求め、実験値と 比べている。計算値は静止した原子の0 "
"Kの最適化構造であり、実験値は各相が安定に存在する 有限温度で測られている。両者の差には、:eq:`ph-thermal-pressure` "
"の熱膨張と零点振動による 体積の増加に加えて、\\ :ref:`交換相関汎関数<exchange-correlation-"
"functional>`\\ の近似によるずれも含まれる。立方晶相は0 Kでは不安定モードをもつので、0 Kの立方晶の格子定数は、 "
"対称性を課して得た鞍点の構造の値である（\\ :ref:`立方晶BaTiO₃の不安定なΓ点モード<phonon-"
"batio3-example>`）。"
msgstr ""
"The `calculation example “Lattice Constants” <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/lattice-constant.html>`_\\  obtains the "
"lattice constants of four phases using DFT (OpenMX, Quantum ESPRESSO) and"
" machine learning interatomic potentials, and compares them with "
"experiment. The calculated values come from optimized structures with "
"static atoms at 0 K, whereas the experimental values are measured at "
"finite temperatures where each phase is stable. The differences include "
"the volume increase due to thermal expansion and zero-point vibrations in"
" Equation :eq:`ph-thermal-pressure`, as well as errors from the "
"approximate \\ :ref:`exchange-correlation functional <exchange-"
"correlation-functional>`\\ . Because the cubic phase has an unstable mode"
" at 0 K, its 0 K lattice constant is that of a saddle-point structure "
"obtained by imposing symmetry (see \\ :ref:`the unstable Γ-point mode of "
"cubic BaTiO₃ <phonon-batio3-example>`)."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:185
msgid ""
"この差のうち、熱膨張と零点振動による部分を準調和近似で見積もれるのは、Γ点の剛体並進を除く全モードの :math:`\\omega^2` "
"が正の構造だけである （\\ :ref:`適用できる条件<qha-applicability>`）。立方晶相は0 "
"Kの計算で虚数振動数をもち、有限温度では大きな振幅の非調和な 運動で平均構造が立方晶に保たれている（\\ :ref:`ソフトモード<soft-"
"mode>`）。そのため、立方晶の構造に式 :eq:`ph-qha-free-energy` を "
"そのまま当てはめて、実験の立方晶の格子定数と比べることはできない。そのような相の格子定数の温度変化は、 \\ :ref:`分子動力学法"
"<molecular-dynamics>`\\ など、非調和な運動を含む有限温度の計算で調べる。ほかの相についても、 "
"準調和近似を使う前に、その相のフォノンに虚数振動数が無いことを確かめる必要がある。事例でも、フォノンによる "
"動的安定性の確認と零点振動の評価を、残る課題に挙げている。"
msgstr ""
"The quasi-harmonic approximation can estimate the contribution of thermal"
" expansion and zero-point vibrations to this difference only for "
"structures with positive :math:`\\omega^2` for all modes except the "
"Γ-point rigid translations (see \\ :ref:`when the approximation applies "
"<qha-applicability>`). The cubic phase has an imaginary frequency in 0 K "
"calculations, whereas at finite temperatures large-amplitude anharmonic "
"motion keeps the average structure cubic (see \\ :ref:`soft modes <soft-"
"mode>`). Thus, Equation :eq:`ph-qha-free-energy` cannot be applied "
"directly to the cubic structure for comparison with the experimental "
"cubic lattice constant. The temperature dependence of the lattice "
"constant of such a phase is studied with finite-temperature calculations "
"that include anharmonic motion, such as \\ :ref:`molecular dynamics "
"<molecular-dynamics>`\\ . Before applying the quasi-harmonic "
"approximation to the other phases, check that their phonons have no "
"imaginary frequencies. The calculation example likewise lists "
"verification of dynamical stability using phonons and evaluation of zero-"
"point vibrations as remaining tasks."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:196
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:198
msgid ""
"本稿の式は、各モードを独立な調和振動子とみなす近似に基づく。準調和近似で取り込む非調和性は振動数の "
"体積依存性だけで、一定体積でのフォノンどうしの相互作用（フォノンの寿命や、振動数の温度依存性）は含まない。 "
"融点に近い高温や、振幅の大きい軽い原子では、これらの効果が無視できなくなる。"
msgstr ""
"The equations in this article treat each mode as an independent harmonic "
"oscillator. The quasi-harmonic approximation includes anharmonicity only "
"through the volume dependence of the frequencies. It leaves out "
"phonon–phonon interactions at fixed volume, including their effects on "
"phonon lifetimes and the temperature dependence of the frequencies. These"
" effects can no longer be neglected at high temperatures near the melting"
" point or for light atoms with large vibrational amplitudes."

#: ../../solid/phonon_thermal.rst:202
msgid ""
"零点振動も、調和近似の範囲では振動数から決まる量として扱った。軽い原子や、浅い二重井戸をもつ系では、原子核の "
"量子揺らぎが非調和なポテンシャルの形に敏感になり、経路積分などで扱う必要がある。"
msgstr ""
"Within the harmonic approximation, we also treated zero-point vibrations "
"as determined by the frequencies. For light atoms or systems with shallow"
" double wells, quantum fluctuations of the nuclei become sensitive to the"
" shape of the anharmonic potential and require a treatment such as path "
"integrals."

